"If revisiting, quick links to <a href=\"#fonttable\">The table of "
"fonts</a> and <a href=\"changelog.html\">Changelog</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><h4>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:33
msgid "Development of this site has ceased!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:35
msgid "For health reasons I am stopping development of this site."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><h4>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:37
msgid "Licensing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:39
msgid ""
"I hope this website will be useful, and I intend that people copy it, "
"or perhaps use it as an example of how <b>NOT</b> to organise things. "
"The layout is derived from my old godaddy website, where everything "
"except the main HTML was below a 'files/' directory. From memory, "
"some of the tools which need to be compiled are explicitly GPL-v2 or "
"GPL-v3. I think that everything else can be regarded as being under "
"the <a href=\"https://opensource.org/license/mit\">MIT License</a>. "
"If I have listed any other licenses for anything except C or C++ "
"code, I now relicense them under the MIT License. Ken Moffat, "
"2025-05-07."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><h4>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:41
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:43
msgid ""
"I am not a typographer, but I've long had an interest in getting good-"
"looking desktop"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:44
msgid ""
"fonts on my Linux desktops, with coverage of everything I'm likely to "
"look at - that"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:45
msgid ""
"nowadays mostly includes text in variants of the Latin alphabet, with "
"some pages in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:46
msgid ""
"Cyrillic alphabets and occasional Greek pages. It also covers fonts, "
"preferably"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:47
msgid ""
"monospaced, for posts on mailing lists. Those posts often include "
"some CJK glyphs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:49
msgid ""
"Despite how many of my posts have included odd misspellings, I "
"usually do know"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:50
msgid ""
"how to spell - but my typing is often poor, with lots of typos (and I "
"find them very"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:51
msgid "hard to spot), so I have called this domain typosetting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:53
msgid ""
"A history of how this has evolved, including my use of TeXLive, and "
"my current"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:54
msgid ""
"thoughts on how I try to style the files showing coverage of "
"languages, is at"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:55
msgid "<a href=\"history.html\">History of my explorations</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:57
msgid ""
"The (consolidated) table of fonts is at <a href=\"#fonttable\">The "
"table of fonts</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:59
msgid ""
"I first started this exercise in about 2011. I have now revised some "
"of the fonts and"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:60
msgid ""
"corrected various errors in my presentation, but that is an ongoing "
"process.  I am"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:61
msgid ""
"reluctant to revisit those fonts for non-Latin/Cyrillic/Greek "
"languages so those old"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:62
msgid ""
"documents are likely to contain typos and may lack capitalisation of "
"proper nouns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:63
msgid "However, I hope to eventually get all CJK fonts revised."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:65
msgid ""
"My aim is to provide details of libre fonts, using PDFs to show the "
"glyphs in each font"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:66
msgid ""
"and to give examples of languages I think the font supports. Where a "
"font provides"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:67
msgid ""
"small capitals I attempt to show those for the languages I use in the "
"examples, and to"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:68
msgid ""
"note any problems with them. AFAICS, unless they are in a separate "
"file it is not possible"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:69
msgid ""
"to use small caps except from LuaLaTeX or XeLaTeX (libreoffice might "
"simulate them)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:70
msgid ""
"Therefore I ignore them in monospace fonts except for the separate "
"caps font of"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:71
msgid "Latin Modern Mono."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:73
msgid ""
"I only look at pre-built fonts: fonts offered as sources use various "
"different tools. When"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:74
msgid ""
"last I looked at Cantarell from Gnome (it appears to be a fork of the "
"original font but"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:75
msgid ""
"retaining the same name) it was only available as source. I have now "
"looked at version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:76
msgid ""
"0.303 which contains a prebuilt font, but that is a variable font and "
"I have no means of"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:77
msgid "discovering what it contains, nor of using it in XeLaTeX."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:79
msgid ""
"I also offer XeLaTeX or LuaLaTeX files from which I created PDFs in "
"the hope that they"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:80
msgid ""
"might occasionally be instructive for other XeLaTeX or LuaLaTeX "
"users. The PDFs for"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:81
msgid ""
"contents ('Glyphs') and some of the lipsum PDFs were created in "
"Libreoffice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:83
msgid ""
"Now that I am starting to use LuaLaTeX for new and revised languages "
"files, the"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:84
msgid ""
"previous versions using XeLaTeX are available at <a href=\"old-"
"xelatex.html\">old-xelatex.html</a>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><h4>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:86
msgid "Links within this site"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:88
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:164
msgid "<a href=\"changelog.html\">Changelog</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:90
msgid "<a href=\"errata.html\">Errata</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:92
msgid ""
"<a href=\"files/PDF-lipsum\">Files of dummy text to compare fonts</"
"a>: The PDF-lipsum directory has various PDFs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:95
msgid ""
"<a href=\"files/lipsum-tex\">Source files for lipsum in XeLaTeX or "
"LuaLaTeX</a> are in files/lipsum-tex."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:97
msgid ""
"<a href=\"files/lipsum-odt\">Very old LibreOffice Writer lipsum "
"source.</a> are in files/lipsum-odt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:99
msgid ""
"<a href=\"cjk-comparisons.html\">Files for comparing CJK fonts</a> :"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:102
msgid ""
"The CJK languages do not usually use dummy text in like Lorem Ipsum."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:103
msgid ""
"Although XeLaTeX has various packages which use real text, they only "
"give"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:104
msgid ""
"provide a limited view of the many available glyphs. I added files to "
"compare"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:105
msgid ""
"codepoints which might differ in CJK fonts. But after looking at a "
"wider range"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:106
msgid ""
"of fonts I now think that sometimes the choices the designer's "
"preference."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:108
msgid ""
"Similarly, I have prepared 'lipsum' files using standard text for "
"variants of"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:109
msgid "Chinese and for Japanese."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:111
msgid ""
"I have also now prepared 'Chinese-fontname-{CN,TW,HK}' files, to "
"compare"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:112
msgid ""
"how different fonts show the same standard text, and to compare how a "
"font"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:113
msgid "renders the standard text in each variant it supports."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:115
msgid ""
"I am now updating the Korean fonts, together with some information on "
"how"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:116
msgid "much, if any, Hanja (Han ideograms) they support."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:125
msgid ""
"Over the last year I have read far too much about experiments which "
"could not be"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:126
msgid ""
"replicated. So, for anyone who wants to access the files I used, "
"including those who"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:127
msgid ""
"merely wish to gain an overview of how I address certain issues in "
"using some of the"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:128
msgid ""
"fonts (typically, related to XeLaTeX or polyglossia), I am putting "
"source files for my"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:129
msgid ""
"tools to determine what is in a font (usage is summarised in <a "
"href=\"current-process.html\">My current process</a>),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:130
msgid ""
"my templates to start identifying which languages a font supports, "
"and the source I"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:131
msgid ""
"have for how I created the lipsum and substitutes files are all "
